{
  "format": "mono 48000 Hz Opus, 96 kbps VBR, zero header gain",
  "rights": "Owner requested the selected professional-library replacements in a public PR in this implementation session. Original masters remain private; retain applicable library entitlement/licence records. Edited media do not inherit the code licence. Review mixes stay local and are not uploaded to the PR.",
  "design": "Owner-selected Blastwave pass-bys 54507 through 54511 only (54504-54506 rejected at audition), material-dependent generic casing drops, family-matched dry-fire donors, isolated cloth throw movements. No synthesized layers or pitch variants. Sand donors stand in for dry earth; carpet for fabric/rubber; concrete for glass/plaster. Casings are not calibre-specific or verified 12-gauge hull recordings. Dry donors are M16, AK47, Glock45, MP5, Remington700 and Pumpgun, not claimed exact recordings of the in-game models. The rejected generic-metal pin donor is removed; pin audio is intentionally silent pending an approved suitable recording. Only these combat-foley paths change; voices, reports, other UI tones, explosions and master safety remain separate. The synthetic grenade cook-warning cue is removed at owner request.",
  "processing": "Decode to mono arithmetic mean, resample 48 kHz, high-pass/low-pass per crop; trim to 5 ms before first 5 ms RMS block exceeding max(-70 dBFS, 4% of peak block RMS), retain the authored crop/tail. 1 ms linear entrance and 10 ms linear exit fades. Scale maximum sliding-window RMS to the listed target subject to -3 dBFS sample-peak headroom. No compression or limiting. Output hashes bind actual Opus files.",
